235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (Bank customer churn is a major challenge where customers close their bank accounts, directly impacting the bank's revenue and growth. This project uses the Bank_Churn dataset to analyze customer demographics, account activity, and behavior patterns. The main aim is to identify factors and patterns that trigger customer churn. SQL queries have been used to explore customer segments, exit rates, and key trends within the data. This analysis will help the bank develop better customer retention strategies.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 203 0 R
/T (Objective)
/E (Objective)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (The objective of this project is to understand customer churn behavior and identify high-risk customer segments. Exit rates have been analyzed based on Age, Gender, and Geography to find patterns. The impact of factors like Credit Score, Balance, and Product usage on churn has also been examined. A comparison between active and inactive members was done to understand engagement patterns. The overall goal is to provide data-driven insights that help improve customer retention.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
